    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> state founded by Turkic-speaking migrants at the confluence of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kama-river">Kama</a> rivers.</li><li>In 922 its ruler adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>, making it the first state of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> with Islam as its official faith.</li><li>It grew rich on northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">furs</a> and Islamic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroyed it in 1236.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chuvash-people">Chuvash</a>, spoken today in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, is the only living language of the Oghuric branch of Turkic, the branch spoken by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Volga Bulgars</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

