ine x1="722.5" x2="722.5" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="722.5" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="722.5" y="164" text-anchor="middle">6</text><title>1223: The Bulgars defeat a Mongol force near the Samara Bend</title></g><g class="rf-ev"><line x1="740.0" x2="740.0" y1="160" y2="166"/><circle cx="740.0" cy="160" r="8"/><text x="740.0" y="164" text-anchor="middle">7</text><title>1236: The Mongols destroy Bilyar and conquer Volga Bulgaria</title></g><text class="rf-axis" x="20" y="200">700 CE</text><text class="rf-axis" x="740" y="200" text-anchor="end">1236 CE</text></svg><figcaption>Relative power on the Institute's 0–10 scale (each profile scaled to its own peak). Numbers mark the key events below.</figcaption></figure><ol class="rf-events"><li><span class="rf-year">c. 700</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> groups move north from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> steppe to the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">922</span><span class="rf-text">Ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alm-s">Almish</a> adopts <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a> during the embassy described by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-fadlan">Ibn Fadlan</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">965</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sviatoslav-i-of-kiev">Sviatoslav I of Kiev</a> breaks <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> power, ending <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> tribute</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">985</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vladimir-the-great">Vladimir of Kiev</a> campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> and makes peace</span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1164</span><span class="rf-text"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-bogolyubsky">Andrei Bogolyubsky</a> of Vladimir-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a> takes the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgar</a> town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bryakhimov">Bryakhimov</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1223</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgars">Bulgars</a> defeat a Mongol force near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-samara-bend">Samara Bend</a></span></li><li><span class="rf-year">1236</span><span class="rf-text">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> destroy <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bilyar">Bilyar</a> and conquer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a></span></li></ol>
